---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1500.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — Who Is a First-Time Adopter" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Common Triggers for First-Time Adoption" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. The General Principle — Retrospective Application" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Mandatory Exceptions to Retrospective Application" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Optional Exemptions — Designed for Cost-Benefit Relief" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. The Opening ASPE Balance Sheet" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Reconciliation Disclosures Required on Transition" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Adjusting Retained Earnings for a Newly Recognized Liability" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — Electing a Business Combination Exemption" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IFRS 1" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A one-time transition framework for entities newly adopting ASPE</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1500 GOVERNS how an ENTERPRISE prepares ITS opening BALANCE sheet and TRANSITIONS to ASPE for the FIRST time — a ROLE conceptually PARALLEL to IFRS 1 internationally, and TO ASBE No. 38 (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster EARLIER in this LIBRARY). Section 1500 INCLUDES various DEFINED exemptions DESIGNED to help a FIRST-time adopter GENERATE financial statements AT a cost that DOES NOT exceed the BENEFITS to users.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Who Is a First-Time Adopter</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Enterprises transitioning from another framework to ASPE</div><div class="principle">A PRIVATE enterprise APPLIES Section 1500 WHEN adopting ASPE for the FIRST time — TYPICALLY as a RESULT of HAVING previously APPLIED IFRS (e.g. FOLLOWING a CHANGE in PUBLIC accountability STATUS), or HAVING prepared FINANCIAL statements under ANOTHER framework NOT in accordance WITH Canadian GAAP.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Common Triggers for First-Time Adoption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Changes in circumstances prompting a transition to ASPE</div><div class="dot-list"><span>A formerly publicly accountable enterprise (previously applying Part I / IFRS) becomes a private enterprise</span><span>An enterprise previously applying a non-Canadian-GAAP framework (e.g. a foreign parent's own GAAP for a Canadian subsidiary) transitions to Canadian GAAP</span><span>An enterprise previously reporting under a compilation or other non-GAAP basis moves to full GAAP-compliant reporting</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The General Principle — Retrospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">As if ASPE had always been applied</div><div class="text-supporting">AS a GENERAL principle, an ENTERPRISE applies ASPE RETROSPECTIVELY in its OPENING balance SHEET, AS IF ASPE had ALWAYS been APPLIED — SUBJECT to SPECIFIC mandatory EXCEPTIONS and OPTIONAL exemptions (Sections 5–6) RECOGNIZING that FULL retrospective APPLICATION would, in CERTAIN areas, be EITHER impracticable OR disproportionately COSTLY for a PRIVATE enterprise.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Mandatory Exceptions to Retrospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Areas where retrospective application is prohibited</div><div class="text-supporting">CERTAIN areas are SPECIFICALLY excluded FROM retrospective APPLICATION — MOST notably, PRIOR derecognition DECISIONS for financial ASSETS and LIABILITIES are GENERALLY not REOPENED, and ESTIMATES made UNDER the PREVIOUS framework are NOT revised WITH the benefit OF hindsight (ESTIMATES must be CONSISTENT with THOSE made AT the same DATE under the PREVIOUS framework, adjusted ONLY for accounting POLICY differences).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Optional Exemptions — Designed for Cost-Benefit Relief</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Practical relief an enterprise may elect</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise MAY elect CERTAIN practical EXEMPTIONS — MOST notably, NOT restating PAST business COMBINATIONS that OCCURRED before the TRANSITION date (RETAINING the PREVIOUS carrying AMOUNTS of goodwill and ACQUIRED assets/LIABILITIES, RATHER than RECALCULATING them UNDER Section 1582'S current ACQUISITION method) — a PRACTICAL relief EXPLICITLY designed to AVOID imposing DISPROPORTIONATE transition COSTS on private ENTERPRISES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>The Opening ASPE Balance Sheet</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The starting point for reporting under the new framework</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise PREPARES an OPENING balance SHEET at the DATE of TRANSITION — RECOGNIZING all ASSETS and LIABILITIES ASPE requires, DERECOGNIZING those it DOES NOT permit, RECLASSIFYING items as NECESSARY, and MEASURING all RECOGNIZED assets and LIABILITIES in ACCORDANCE with ASPE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Reconciliation Disclosures Required on Transition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Bridging the old framework's results to ASPE</div><div class="text-supporting">A FIRST-time adopter DISCLOSES a RECONCILIATION of ITS equity and NET income UNDER the PREVIOUS framework to THOSE same FIGURES under ASPE — HELPING readers UNDERSTAND the FINANCIAL statement IMPACT of the TRANSITION. (SINCE ASPE has NO Other Comprehensive INCOME concept, THIS reconciliation FOCUSES on NET income, RATHER than a BROADER "comprehensive INCOME" figure, WHICH WOULD be RELEVANT under an EQUIVALENT IFRS reconciliation.)</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Adjusting Retained Earnings for a Newly Recognized Liability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognizing a liability the previous framework did not require</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Recognizing an asset retirement obligation for the first time</div><div class="wk-body">A company transitioning to ASPE previously applied a framework with no asset retirement obligation guidance. On transition, it identifies a legal obligation requiring recognition of a $600,000 asset retirement obligation liability (see the future companion Section 3110 poster) under ASPE.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RECOGNIZES the $600,000 LIABILITY in its OPENING balance SHEET, WITH a CORRESPONDING adjustment REDUCING opening RETAINED earnings (or, WHERE appropriate, ADJUSTING the RELATED asset) by <strong>$600,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Electing a Business Combination Exemption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Retaining previous carrying amounts rather than restating</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Not restating a pre-transition acquisition</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquired a subsidiary four years before its ASPE transition date, recognizing goodwill under its previous framework's own measurement approach.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company ELECTS the BUSINESS combination EXEMPTION, RETAINING the PREVIOUS carrying AMOUNT of GOODWILL as its OPENING ASPE balance, RATHER than RECALCULATING the ACQUISITION under SECTION 1582'S current ACQUISITION method.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1500 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Reconciliation of equity and net income from the previous framework to ASPE</span><span>Nature of any exemptions elected on transition</span><span>Explanation of material adjustments made to the opening balance sheet</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Which optional exemptions to elect on transition, balancing cost-benefit considerations</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimates used in the opening balance sheet must be consistent with estimates made at that date under the previous framework, adjusted only for accounting policy differences</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 1</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1500 vs IFRS 1</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1500</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 1</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>General retrospective principle</span><span>YES, with exceptions/exemptions</span><span>YES, with exceptions/exemptions — conceptually parallel</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Business combination exemption</span><span>Available</span><span>Available — converged in spirit</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY conceptually PARALLEL standard, TAILORED specifically to the COST-benefit needs of a PRIVATE enterprise TRANSITIONING to a SIMPLER, less COMPLEX reporting FRAMEWORK than IFRS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every transition adjustment lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Opening balance sheet adjustment</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge sre">SRE</span></span><span>Typically adjusted through opening retained earnings</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1582</span><span>Business Combinations — the standard this Section's optional business combination exemption relates to</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Date of transition</div><div class="glossary-def">The beginning of the earliest period for which an enterprise presents full comparative information under ASPE for the first time.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Opening ASPE Balance Sheet</div><div class="glossary-def">The Balance Sheet prepared at the date of transition, forming the starting point for reporting under ASPE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1500 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
